CHANGELOG.md:302:| `as` on an import of a module that declares built-in effects (`IO.Console`, `IO.File`, `IO.Process`, `IO.Clock`, `IO.Random`, `Network.Http`, `IO`, `Assert`), such as `import Benitoite.Unofficial.IO.File as Console`, also when the new name is the original one | `E0339` | Remove `as` and refer to the module by its own name, such as `File.readText` and `uses File.Read`. If the name collides with another import, rename the other import. The alias could make `uses` show an effect name that does not match the operation, such as `uses Console.Write` for writing files. |
crates/benitoite/skill/SKILL.md:128:- Import every module outside the prelude, also when it only appears in `uses`. Unofficial modules (all IO and network modules, `Json`, `Csv`, and others) are imported under `Benitoite.Unofficial`: `import Benitoite.Unofficial.IO.Console`, then referred to as `Console`. `import Benitoite.IO.Console` is an error. The unofficial modules are `IO.Console`, `IO.File`, `IO.Process`, `IO.Clock`, `IO.Random`, `Network.Http`, `Json`, `Json.Codec`, `Failure`, `Test.Property`, `Csv`, `Regex`, `Scope`, `Range`, `NonEmptyList`, `Log`, `SourceLocation`, `Path`, `Time`, `Encoding`, and `Hash`; for example `import Benitoite.Unofficial.Network.Http` is referred to as `Http`. Do not rename the modules that declare effects (the IO and network modules, `IO`, `Log`, and `Assert`) with `as`; that is an error, so that `uses` always shows the real effect names.
